### 12.7 Deep semantic review of `leviCivitaExists` (closure CONFIRMED)

Reviewed the mathematics, not only the compilation:
- Koszul derivation gives `∇_X Y = ½([X,Y] − (ad_X)^T Y − (ad_Y)^T X)`; this is exactly
  `milnorConnection`.
- Torsion: adjoint terms cancel pairwise, leaving `∇_X Y − ∇_Y X = [X,Y]`; uses only
  bracket skew-symmetry, matching `milnorConnection_torsionFree`.
- Compatibility: substituting the formula gives
  `⟨∇_X Y,Z⟩ + ⟨Y,∇_X Z⟩ = −½(⟨(ad_Y)^T X,Z⟩ + ⟨Y,(ad_Z)^T X⟩) = −½(⟨X,[Y,Z]⟩ − ⟨X,[Y,Z]⟩) = 0`,
  using only metric symmetry and bracket skew, matching
  `milnorConnection_metricCompatible`.
- Uniqueness `leviCivita_nabla_unique` is the standard symmetric-antisymmetric argument
  with nondegeneracy; reviewed.
Scope note (not a defect): `IsMetricCompatible` in the D2 interface is the algebraic
*left-invariant* condition `⟨∇_X Y,Z⟩ + ⟨Y,∇_X Z⟩ = 0` (no directional-derivative term).
The closure is of the blocker as recorded; the general Koszul/manifold theorem is a
different statement. Upstream DoCarmo Ch. 2 supplies the general statement (source claim).
