dsh: reasoning:
The covering recognition proof looks solid:
- For each e, the nontrivial translates g•e are at positive distance d_g from e (freeness).
- Continuity gives η_g such that points within η_g of e map within d_g/2 of g•e.
- δ = min over nontrivial g of min(η_g, d_g/2) > 0.
- Then for any nontrivial g, the ball B(e,δ) is disjoint from its g-translate: if u ∈ B(e,δ) and g•u ∈ B(e,δ), then dist(g•u, g•e) < d_g/2 (since dist(u,e)<δ≤η_g) and dist(g•e, e) = d_g; triangle gives d_g ≤ dist(g•e, g•u) + dist(g•u, e) < d_g/2 + δ ≤ d_g/2 + d_g/2 = d_g, contradiction. Wait: δ ≤ val g ≤ d_g/2, so dist(g•u,e) < δ ≤ d_g/2. Then d_g ≤ dist(g•e, g•u) + dist(g•u, e) < d_g/2 + d_g/2 = d_g — contradiction. ✓

